  "body": "Perched high within the beautifully landscaped surrounds of Kensington Park, this exceptional two-bedroom penthouse offers a wonderful sense of privacy, space and serenity. Elevated above the everyday, it's a home that invites you to slow down and enjoy the little things - from the gentle sound of rain falling on the roof to the feeling of complete privacy that makes this apartment such a peaceful retreat.\r\n\r\nThe expansive deck is where this home truly comes into its own. Generous in scale and perfectly positioned to capture the afternoon sun, it creates an enviable outdoor living space for enjoying morning coffee, entertaining friends or simply settling in as the day winds down. With its elevated position and leafy outlook, there is a wonderful sense of being removed from the world, while still having everything Kensington Park has to offer right on your doorstep.\r\n\r\nInside, the two-bedroom layout provides an elegant and effortless base for coastal living, combining the privacy and convenience of penthouse living with the beauty of its park-like surroundings. Just moments from Orewa Beach, village cafés and restaurants, and with the motorway on-ramp conveniently nearby, this is a home that makes everyday living wonderfully easy.\r\n\r\nPrivate, peaceful and bathed in afternoon sun - this is elevated coastal living at its finest.\r\n\r\nAs a resident of Kensington Park, you'll also enjoy access to an exceptional range of community amenities designed to complement the way you live. Take a dip in the heated indoor swimming pool, keep active in the fully equipped gym, or unwind in the sauna. Beyond the apartment, the extensive landscaped gardens provide beautiful spaces to wander, with walking tracks winding through native bush, while the golden sands of Orewa Beach are just moments away.\r\n\r\nThis is a rare opportunity to enjoy living within one of Orewa's most distinctive residential communities.\r\n\r\nContact Sandra or Tonia in the onsite sales suite.\r\nKensington Park Realty, Licensed REAA 2008.",
